{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kku9HUMgoEa5nXDieU17np","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→id: rel00.0-uc003-sys\n     2→title: \"Query terminal width, stat files, and handle signals via pkg/sys\"\n     3→\n     4→summary: |\n     5→  The operator verifies that pkg/sys provides correct terminal-width queries, extended\n     6→  file metadata, and signal handling on both Darwin and Linux. The test exercises each\n     7→  capability in isolation: TerminalWidth returns a positive column count on a TTY,\n     8→  IsTerminal distinguishes terminals from pipes, Stat and Lstat return correct extended\n     9→  metadata, InstallSIGPIPEHandler suppresses broken-pipe errors, and OnTerminalResize\n    10→  invokes callbacks on SIGWINCH.\n    11→\n    12→actor: Human Operator\n    13→\n    14→trigger: |\n    15→  The operator has completed the PRD revision (prd002-sys.yaml) and wants to verify that\n    16→  pkg/sys satisfies its requirements via unit tests.\n    17→\n    18→flow:\n    19→  - id: F1\n    20→    step: |\n    21→      The operator runs go test ./pkg/sys/... which executes the unit tests for pkg/sys.\n    22→      Unlike cmd/ packages, pkg/sys does not use differential testing because there is no\n    23→      reference binary — it is a library.\n    24→  - id: F2\n    25→    step: |\n    26→      The TerminalWidth test calls TerminalWidth() and verifies it returns a positive\n    27→      integer when stdout is a terminal, or an error when stdout is a pipe.\n    28→  - id: F3\n    29→    step: |\n    30→      The IsTerminal test calls IsTerminal with a pipe fd and verifies it returns false.\n    31→      It calls IsTerminal with a TTY fd (if available in the test environment) and verifies\n    32→      it returns true.\n    33→  - id: F4\n    34→    step: |\n    35→      The Stat test calls Stat on a known file and verifies Nlink, Uid, Gid, Dev, Ino,\n    36→      and Blocks match the output of stat(1) on the same file.\n    37→  - id: F5\n    38→    step: |\n    39→      The Lstat test calls Lstat on a symbolic link and verifies that the returned FileInfo\n    40→      has type bits showing symlink, not the target's mode.\n    41→  - id: F6\n    42→    step: |\n    43→      The fillFromStat test verifies that the Darwin/Linux abstraction correctly populates\n    44→      FileInfo.ModTime from st_mtimespec (Darwin) or st_mtim (Linux).\n    45→  - id: F7\n    46→    step: |\n    47→      The InstallSIGPIPEHandler test verifies that writing to a broken pipe after installing\n    48→      the handler causes the process to exit 0 rather than printing a write error.\n    49→\n    50→touchpoints:\n    51→  - T1: \"pkg/sys — TerminalWidth, IsTerminal (prd002-sys R1)\"\n    52→  - T2: \"pkg/sys — Stat, Lstat, FileInfo, fillFromStat (prd002-sys R2)\"\n    53→  - T3: \"pkg/sys — InstallSIGPIPEHandler (prd002-sys R3)\"\n    54→  - T4: \"pkg/sys — OnTerminalResize (prd002-sys R4)\"\n    55→\n    56→success_criteria:\n    57→  - id: S1\n    58→    criterion: TerminalWidth returns a positive integer on a TTY or an error on a pipe.\n    59→  - id: S2\n    60→    criterion: IsTerminal(pipeFd) returns false.\n    61→  - id: S3\n    62→    criterion: Stat on a known file returns correct Nlink, Uid, Gid, Dev, Ino, Blocks.\n    63→  - id: S4\n    64→    criterion: Lstat on a symlink returns type bits showing symlink.\n    65→  - id: S5\n    66→    criterion: FileInfo.ModTime is populated from the platform-correct field.\n    67→  - id: S6\n    68→    criterion: InstallSIGPIPEHandler causes exit 0 on broken pipe.\n    69→  - id: S7\n    70→    criterion: go test ./pkg/sys/... passes on darwin/arm64 with no failures.\n    71→\n    72→out_of_scope:\n    73→  - SIGWINCH testing requires a real terminal resize event; it is tested manually, not in the harness.\n    74→  - Process-group management (setpgid, killpg) is deferred to the xargs PRD.\n    75→  - SIGUSR1/SIGUSR2 handling is deferred to the find PRD.\n    76→\n    77→test_suite: test-rel00.0\n    78→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c04ec8d-e461-4313-9643-b8fba7f8d3f9","uuid":"8227f329-3af5-4e95-8ab8-5b191108fdfa","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/123/docs/specs/use-cases/rel00.0-uc003-sys.yaml","content":"id: rel00.0-uc003-sys\ntitle: \"Query terminal width, stat files, and handle signals via pkg/sys\"\n\nsummary: |\n  The operator verifies that pkg/sys provides correct terminal-width queries, extended\n  file metadata, and signal handling on both Darwin and Linux. The test exercises each\n  capability in isolation: TerminalWidth returns a positive column count on a TTY,\n  IsTerminal distinguishes terminals from pipes, Stat and Lstat return correct extended\n  metadata, InstallSIGPIPEHandler suppresses broken-pipe errors, and OnTerminalResize\n  invokes callbacks on SIGWINCH.\n\nactor: Human Operator\n\ntrigger: |\n  The operator has completed the PRD revision (prd002-sys.yaml) and wants to verify that\n  pkg/sys satisfies its requirements via unit tests.\n\nflow:\n  - id: F1\n    step: |\n      The operator runs go test ./pkg/sys/... which executes the unit tests for pkg/sys.\n      Unlike cmd/ packages, pkg/sys does not use differential testing because there is no\n      reference binary — it is a library.\n  - id: F2\n    step: |\n      The TerminalWidth test calls TerminalWidth() and verifies it returns a positive\n      integer when stdout is a terminal, or an error when stdout is a pipe.\n  - id: F3\n    step: |\n      The IsTerminal test calls IsTerminal with a pipe fd and verifies it returns false.\n      It calls IsTerminal with a TTY fd (if available in the test environment) and verifies\n      it returns true.\n  - id: F4\n    step: |\n      The Stat test calls Stat on a known file and verifies Nlink, Uid, Gid, Dev, Ino,\n      and Blocks match the output of stat(1) on the same file.\n  - id: F5\n    step: |\n      The Lstat test calls Lstat on a symbolic link and verifies that the returned FileInfo\n      has type bits showing symlink, not the target's mode.\n  - id: F6\n    step: |\n      The fillFromStat test verifies that the Darwin/Linux abstraction correctly populates\n      FileInfo.ModTime from st_mtimespec (Darwin) or st_mtim (Linux).\n  - id: F7\n    step: |\n      The InstallSIGPIPEHandler test verifies that writing to a broken pipe after installing\n      the handler causes the process to exit 0 rather than printing a write error.\n\ntouchpoints:\n  - T1: \"pkg/sys — TerminalWidth, IsTerminal (prd002-sys R1)\"\n  - T2: \"pkg/sys — Stat, Lstat, FileInfo, fillFromStat (prd002-sys R2)\"\n  - T3: \"pkg/sys — InstallSIGPIPEHandler (prd002-sys R3)\"\n  - T4: \"pkg/sys — OnTerminalResize (prd002-sys R4)\"\n\nsuccess_criteria:\n  - id: S1\n    criterion: TerminalWidth returns a positive integer on a TTY or an error on a pipe.\n  - id: S2\n    criterion: IsTerminal(pipeFd) returns false.\n  - id: S3\n    criterion: Stat on a known file returns correct Nlink, Uid, Gid, Dev, Ino, Blocks.\n  - id: S4\n    criterion: Lstat on a symlink returns type bits showing symlink.\n  - id: S5\n    criterion: FileInfo.ModTime is populated from the platform-correct field.\n  - id: S6\n    criterion: InstallSIGPIPEHandler causes exit 0 on broken pipe.\n  - id: S7\n    criterion: go test ./pkg/sys/... passes on darwin/arm64 with no failures.\n\nout_of_scope:\n  - SIGWINCH testing requires a real terminal resize event; it is tested manually, not in the harness.\n  - Process-group management (setpgid, killpg) is deferred to the xargs PRD.\n  - SIGUSR1/SIGUSR2 handling is deferred to the find PRD.\n\ntest_suite: test-rel00.0\n","numLines":78,"startLine":1,"totalLines":78}}}
